{"id":"evt_seedAmaraHeadache0058","sessionId":"ses_seedAmaraHeadache","seq":58,"at":"2026-09-29T21:14:59.978Z","type":"turn.end","payload":{"messageId":"msg_seedA07","status":"complete","usage":{"tokensIn":1350,"tokensCached":0,"tokensOut":116,"costUsd":0.000152,"energySpent":2,"firstTokenMs":2257,"totalMs":2963},"citations":[{"n":1,"sourceId":"kno_seedAmara2","title":"ED triage guidelines","type":"file","chunkId":"kch_amaraTri10","locator":"p. 3","quote":"## 3. Red flags\n\n## 3.1 Escalate at once\n\nEscalate any headache that is sudden and severe (\"thunderclap\"), or that comes with fever, neck stiffness, confusion, new weakness or changes in vision.","score":0.895},{"n":2,"sourceId":"kno_seedAmara2","title":"ED triage guidelines","type":"file","chunkId":"kch_amaraTri11","locator":"p. 3","quote":"## 3.2 Other warning signs\n\n- A headache with a rash that does not fade under pressure: grade 1.","score":0.58},{"n":3,"sourceId":"kno_seedAmara2","title":"ED triage guidelines","type":"file","chunkId":"kch_amaraTri12","locator":"p. 3","quote":"## 3.3 Same-day review\n\nA first severe headache after age 50, a headache after a head injury, or one that wakes the patient from sleep should also be reviewed the same day, even when observations are normal.","score":0.54}]}},
